(THE STORY IN ONE MINUTE) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(SAHAYAK aims to make a small set of recognized signs visible as text, with speech support,) Tj
T*
(through a web interface.) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(The problem: communication between a sign-language user and someone unfamiliar with signs) Tj
T*
(can be difficult. A digital tool may help in some everyday situations, but it is not a) Tj
T*
(replacement for interpreters or full language access.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Current flow: camera -> MediaPipe Hands detects hand landmarks in the browser -> the) Tj
T*
(website converts landmarks into numeric features -> the backend model predicts a supported) Tj
T*
(label -> the page shows text. Speech and translation are separate features that may) Tj
T*
(require internet.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Static two-hand path: 126 values. Continuous-sequence path: 132 values per frame across 10) Tj
T*
(time bins, for 1320 values.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(The current label set should be checked on /api/status before presenting. Project labels) Tj
T*
(have included HELLO, I_LOVE_YOU, NO, THANK_YOU, and YES; do not promise every sign in ISL.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Core honesty rule: say 'prototype' and 'supported signs', not 'complete ISL translator'.) Tj
T*
(No verified model-accuracy figure is supplied in this guide.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
