(SPEAKER 1 | SHYAMANTIKA PEGU) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(ROLE: OPENING, PROBLEM, PURPOSE AND PROJECT SCOPE) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Target time: 1 minute 30 seconds) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(SAY:) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Good morning respected judges, teachers, and everyone present here. We are presenting our) Tj
T*
(project SAHAYAK, a real-time Indian Sign Language recognition system.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(The word 'Sahayak' means helper. Our idea is to explore how computer vision and machine) Tj
T*
(learning can support communication between a person using signs and a person who may not) Tj
T*
(understand those signs.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Communication barriers can affect classrooms, public services, and everyday conversations.) Tj
T*
(Sign languages are real languages, but many people around a sign-language user may not) Tj
T*
(know them. Our project explores one small technological aid for this situation.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Our goal is not to replace sign-language interpreters, teach a complete language, or claim) Tj
T*
(that a computer can understand every sign. We are building a prototype that recognizes a) Tj
T*
(limited set of signs and displays the predicted label as text. The website also includes) Tj
T*
(speech and translation features.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(We will explain how it works, show the current prototype, and discuss its limitations and) Tj
T*
(future improvements.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(DO / SHOW: Display the homepage and point to the project title. Keep this opening slow and) Tj
T*
(confident.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(HAND-OFF: Now that we have explained why we chose this problem, Barakha will explain the) Tj
T*
(system and how the recognition pipeline works.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
