(SPEAKER 1 | BACKUP NOTES) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(KEY TERMS) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Computer vision: software that analyses images or video frames.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Landmark: a key point on a hand, such as a fingertip or joint.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Feature: a number that represents useful information from the detected hand.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Classifier: a trained model that chooses among the labels it has learned.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Real-time: the system processes new camera frames while the session is running. Actual) Tj
T*
(speed depends on device, network, and server.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(WHY THIS PROJECT MATTERS) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(It can be used as a learning prototype, a demonstration of accessible technology, and a) Tj
T*
(starting point for a better-tested sign-recognition tool.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(DO NOT SAY) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(- It recognizes every Indian Sign Language sentence.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(- It is 98% or 99% accurate unless a valid evaluation proves that.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(- It works fully offline. Model inference, translation, or speech may depend on backend or) Tj
T*
(internet.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(- It replaces interpreters or guarantees correct communication.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(IF ASKED 'WHY SAHAYAK?') Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(We chose the name because the project is intended to act as a helper. Technology should) Tj
T*
(support accessibility while respecting that sign languages and Deaf communities are much) Tj
T*
(more than a list of gestures.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
