(SPEAKER 2 | BARAKHA DOLEY) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(ROLE: ARCHITECTURE, AI AND WEBSITE FEATURES) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Target time: 2 minutes) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(SAY:) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Thank you, Shyamantika. I will explain how SAHAYAK works.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(First, the user opens the website and allows camera access. The browser uses MediaPipe) Tj
T*
(Hands to detect hand landmarks. Instead of sending the whole camera image to the) Tj
T*
(classifier, the current interface extracts numeric hand coordinates and turns them into) Tj
T*
(features.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(For the static two-hand model, the feature vector contains 126 values: 21 landmarks for) Tj
T*
(each of two hands, with three coordinates per landmark. These numbers are sent to our) Tj
T*
(Flask backend, where a scikit-learn model saved with Joblib predicts one of its supported) Tj
T*
(labels.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(The project also has a continuous-sign pathway. It collects a sequence of frames,) Tj
T*
(represents each frame with 132 values, and resamples the sequence into 10 time bins. That) Tj
T*
(creates a 1320-value input for the sequence model. This is intended for signs where) Tj
T*
(movement over time matters, although results depend on the trained model and quality of) Tj
T*
(the sequence.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(The website displays the predicted sign as text. Translation and speech are additional) Tj
T*
(functions; they are not the same thing as recognizing the hand movement. Some of these) Tj
T*
(services need an internet connection.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(In short, the system combines browser-based hand tracking, numeric feature extraction, a) Tj
T*
(backend machine-learning model, and a website interface.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(DO / SHOW: Use a simple diagram or point through the homepage and Live Studio. Do not) Tj
T*
(start the demo yet.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(HAND-OFF: Himanghsu will now demonstrate the live website and explain what the audience) Tj
T*
(should look for.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
