(SPEAKER 2 | TECHNICAL CHEAT SHEET) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(PIPELINE) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(1. Camera: captures the user's hand movement after permission is granted.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(2. MediaPipe Hands: estimates hand landmarks in the browser.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(3. Feature extraction: converts landmarks into numeric input.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(4. Backend API: receives features and runs the model.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(5. Classifier: selects a label from the classes it knows.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(6. Interface: displays the prediction; speech or translation can be requested separately.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(IMPORTANT DIMENSIONS) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Static path: 126 features = 2 hands x 21 landmarks x 3 coordinates.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Sequence path: 132 values per frame x 10 time bins = 1320 values.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(TECH STACK) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript and browser-side MediaPipe Hands.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Backend: Python Flask API.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Machine learning: scikit-learn model artifacts saved with Joblib.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Hosting: frontend on Vercel; backend on Render.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(WHAT THE MODEL DOES NOT DO) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(The model does not automatically learn a new sign because a label is typed into a JSON) Tj
T*
(file. New signs require labeled data, training, evaluation, and deployment of a new model) Tj
T*
(artifact.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(IF ASKED 'WHY NOT JUST USE IMAGES?') Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(This version uses hand landmarks as a compact numeric representation. It may reduce) Tj
T*
(dependence on raw image appearance, but can miss facial expression, body posture, and) Tj
T*
(context important in sign language.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
