(JUDGE Q&A | PART 1) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(Q1. What is SAHAYAK?) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: A web-based prototype using hand landmarks and machine learning to recognize a limited) Tj
T*
(set of signs and display predicted labels.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q2. What problem does it address?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: It explores a technological aid where someone may not understand a sign-language user's) Tj
T*
(signs. It is not a replacement for interpreters.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q3. What is MediaPipe?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: A framework that can detect hand landmarks from camera frames. Here, landmark detection) Tj
T*
(runs in the browser.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q4. What is a landmark?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: A key point on a hand, such as a joint or fingertip, represented by coordinates.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q5. Why use machine learning?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: The classifier learns patterns in labeled examples and predicts which supported class) Tj
T*
(is most similar to a new feature vector.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q6. Which language and framework are used on the backend?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Python with Flask for the API; the classifier uses scikit-learn and Joblib model files.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q7. Does it understand all ISL?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: No. It recognizes only a limited set of trained labels. It is not a complete ISL) Tj
T*
(translator.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q8. What does real-time mean here?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: It processes camera frames during a live session. Response time varies with device,) Tj
T*
(network, and backend.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
