/F1 18 Tf
(JUDGE Q&A | PART 2) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(Q9. Why are there 126 features?) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Two hands x 21 landmarks per hand x 3 coordinates per landmark equals 126 values.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q10. Why is there a sequence model?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Some signs depend on movement over time, so a sequence can represent more than a single) Tj
T*
(hand pose. Success still depends on data and training.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q11. Does the project work offline?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Not fully. Some browser-side functions can run after loading, but backend prediction,) Tj
T*
(translation, or speech may require connectivity.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q12. How do you know its accuracy?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Report accuracy only after a documented test on held-out examples, ideally separated by) Tj
T*
(signer or recording session. We do not claim an unverified percentage.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q13. How will you add a new sign?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Define the label, collect diverse labeled samples, train a candidate model, evaluate it) Tj
T*
(against old and new signs, update label metadata and model artifact, then deploy and test.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q14. Is typing a new label enough?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: No. The model must be trained on examples of that sign. A label file alone does not) Tj
T*
(teach the model.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q15. What are the main limitations?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Limited signs, possible errors, sensitivity to recording conditions, network dependence) Tj
T*
(for some features, and missing context such as facial expression and grammar.) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Q16. How do you protect users?) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(A: Ask for camera permission, explain data processing, avoid retaining video) Tj
T*
(unnecessarily, and get informed consent for training data.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
